Package: rothRmel
Type: Package
Title: Rothermel Surface and Van Wagner Crown Fire Behavior from TLS Fuels
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Scott", "Pokswinski", email = "spokswinski@newmexicoconsortium.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The fire behavior calculations behind the rothRmel tab of the
    IntELiMon Decision Support Tool, as plain R functions. Estimates surface
    fire spread and reaction intensity with the Rothermel (1972) model as
    described by Andrews (2018), fireline intensity and flame length after
    Byram (1959), crown fire initiation and active crown fire thresholds after
    Van Wagner (1977), crown fire spread after Rothermel (1991), torching and
    crowning indices after Scott and Reinhardt (2001), and downed woody fuel
    loads from planar intersect counts after Brown (1974). Intended for change
    tracking and treatment success with fuels derived from terrestrial laser
    scanning (TLS), not for operational fire behavior prediction.
